"## Summary\n\nIsolation follow-up 18: session launched 08:38 EST on 2026-11-03 on #422's `main` (`090bb97b`), and delivered at 09:52. One documents-only correction, on the same conversation, ran from 09:57 to 10:07.\n- **Model:** agy `gemini-4-argon-high`.\n- **Size:** 3 commits and 274 owned files, +340,099/−92,590. Almost all of it is evidence: follow-up 17's archived root snapshot (138 files), and the new run's root evidence and stream archive.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes. No Docker object is left.\n  - The orchestrator reran the new Go regression, the D-098 archive pins and the D-144 tests: all pass.\n  - The orchestrator also ran the new Python test against `main`'s review script: it fails there, and passes on this branch.\n- **Scope:** no workflow triggered, re-run or dispatched, and no reservation.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **The run:** scheduled run 41640196805 (on `main` `487c698e`, 11-03) failed as D-144 requires. Four rows blocked, two of them unlisted.\n- **One cause for both.** `deadline()` restarted control and the worker in a deferred `docker start`, and nothing waited for readiness.\n  - **AT13, short whole-node lease expiry.**\n    - The next row's admin login went through the gateway while control was still starting. It got a 502, 406.6 ms after the restart; control served its first request about 7.9 s later.\n    - The deferred pre-enrollment fleet audit hit the same 502. It is a consequence, not a second cause.\n  - **AT10, foreign ingress redirect.**\n    - The harness waited 0 s. It read a readiness record that only `waitControl` writes, and no step had called it.\n    - The agent's records show its retry queue drained, and current observations accepted from 17.2 s before the check.\n  - **Why only on the runner:** locally, control restarts fast enough to hide this. This is a harness defect, not runner slowness and not a product defect.\n- **The previous night's run